# Canonical identity for this project.
#
# Every commit in this repository is by the same author. Some early commits were made under
# addresses that were not the project's working address -- a personal account, and GitHub's
# per-account noreply. This file declares the canonical one, which is the address on the
# OpenPGP release-signing key B128 526A F85A E4A8 F22B  949F B014 5F74 B78C F1DA.
#
# Git honours this for `git shortlog`, `git log --use-mailmap`, and most tooling built on them.
#
# HISTORY IS NOT REWRITTEN, deliberately. Rewriting would change every commit hash, invalidate
# the signed tags, break the Radicle refs, and orphan what Software Heritage has already archived
# -- and it would not even achieve the aim, because GitHub retains unreferenced objects and a
# force-push does not unpublish what was already fetched, forked, or indexed. Declaring the
# canonical identity is both the honest fix and the effective one.
#
# A superseded personal address is deliberately NOT enumerated here. Listing it would publish it
# in a tracked, searchable file -- a fresh, more legible copy of exactly the thing being retired.
# The explanation belongs in the open; the address does not.

parthod0x <parthms.id@gmail.com> <parthod0x@users.noreply.github.com>
parthod0x <parthms.id@gmail.com> <parthms.id@gmail.com>
